<title>BELGIUM: Delhaize jumps on Food Lion, dollar.</title>
<headline>Delhaize jumps on Food Lion, dollar.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Belgian retailer Delhaize jumped more than three percent in Brussels on Wednesday, mainly on the recent strong performance by its U.S. unit Food Lion and a solid dollar, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0830 GMT, Delhaize was up 2.0 percent at 1,820 francs after earlier touching a new high of 1,840 -- up 3.4 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a combination of some Bel-20 index basket buying, Food Lion, the dollar, a recent buy recommendation for Food Lion by Morgan Stanley and some switching from (fellow retailer) GIB to Delhaize,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
